<page class="methodology-page">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>

    <h2>Testing Approach</h2>
    {{#blackBox}}
    <h3>Black Box Testing</h3>
    <p>The assessor starts with no prior knowledge of the target beyond publicly available identifiers such as IP addresses, hostnames, or URLs — simulating an external attacker.</p>
    {{/blackBox}}

    {{#grayBox}}
    <h3>Gray Box Testing</h3>
    <p>The assessor works with partial knowledge of the target, supplemented by information supplied by the client, widening the tested surface to authenticated workflows and internal enumeration.</p>
    {{/grayBox}}

    {{#whiteBox}}
    <h3>White Box Testing</h3>
    <p>The assessor has full visibility into the system under test, including source code and configuration, enabling deep analysis of design-level weaknesses.</p>
    {{/whiteBox}}

